  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 238 PM MDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nFor the long term period, active weather continues for south \ncentral and southeastern Colorado. The favorable monsoon pattern\nwill continue for the region, with the high pressure remaining \nto the southeast, and moist southwesterly flow continuing to \nstream over the area. With that said, there may be some wobble \nin the location of the high pressure early next week, but model \nguidance is in decent agreement with keeping moist flow in \nplace, leading to better confidence in the forecast. So, with \nthis pattern in place, daily showers and thunderstorms are \nexpected, with heavy rain, gusty outflow winds, and frequent \nlightning the main hazards. In addition, flash flooding may \nbecome a concern heading into this period due to both slow \nmoving thunderstorms and the potential for areas to receive \nmultiple rounds of heavy rain on different days. Otherwise, \nwinds are expected to remain light outside of thunderstorms, \nwith increased cloud cover during the afternoon and evening \nhours. Looking at temperatures, much of the region will cool to \naround and below seasonal values for mid August.",
